                      </div>
                    </div>
                  ))}
                </div>

                {/* 90-Day GTM Plan */}
                <div style={{ background: D.card, border: `1px solid ${D.border}`, borderRadius: 14, padding: 24 }}>
                  <h3 style={{ margin: "0 0 14px 0", fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 800, color: D.slate1 }}>90-Day GTM Plan</h3>
                  {[
                    { phase: "Days 1-30", title: "Launch Phase", color: D.purple, items: ["Product Hunt launch â target Top 5 of the day", "Free plan: 2 audits/mo â drives zero-risk trial signups", "Founder LinkedIn content: 3x/week before/after CRO teardowns with real URLs", "Target: 500 free signups + 30 paying customers ($1,770 MRR)"] },
                    { phase: "Days 31-60", title: "Content Engine", color: D.blue, items: ["SEO articles: 'CRO audit checklist', 'landing page analyzer free' (high intent keywords)", "Reddit engagement: r/entrepreneur, r/SaaS, r/digital_marketing with genuine value posts", "YouTube: 3-minute URL audit walkthroughs (compounding SEO value)", "Target: 150 paying customers ($8,850 MRR)"] },
                    { phase: "Days 61-90", title: "Referral + Agency", color: D.green, items: ["Agency partner program launch: 20% commission on referred customer revenue", "Productized 'agency bundle' promotion: 3 months Growth for price of 2", "Guest posts on CRO/conversion blogs: Unbounce, CXL, ConversionXL", "Target: 280 paying customers ($16,520 MRR)"] },
                  ].map(p => (
                    <div key={p.phase} style={{ marginBottom: 16 }}>
                      <div style={{ display: "flex", gap: 8, alignItems: "center", marginBottom: 8 }}>
                        <span style={{ background: p.color + "20", color: p.color, borderRadius: 6, padding: "2px 10px", fontSize: 11, fontWeight: 700 }}>{p.phase}</span>
                        <span style={{ fontWeight: 700, fontSize: 13, color: D.slate1 }}>{p.title}</span>
                      </div>
                      {p.items.map(item => <div key={item} style={{ fontSize: 12, color: D.slate2, marginBottom: 4, paddingLeft: 14 }}>â¢ {item}</div>)}
                    </div>
                  ))}
                </div>
              </div>

              {/* Revenue Streams */}
              <h3 style={{ fontSize: 18, fontWeight: 800, color: D.slate1, margin: "28px 0 18px 0" }}>Revenue Streams Beyond Subscriptions</h3>
              <div style={{ display: "grid", gridTemplateColumns: "repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr))", gap: 16 }}>
                {[
                  { icon: "â¡", title: "Audit Credits Top-Ups", value: "$9 / 10 audits", desc: "Starter users who hit monthly limits can purchase packs. Estimated 15% of Starter users buy 1+ packs/mo. [assumption]", color: D.purple },
                  { icon: "ð·ï¸", title: "White-Label License", value: "$199/mo Agency", desc: "10 seats + client portal + custom branding. Agencies cross-sell to all clients â high LTV, low churn. [assumption]", color: D.amber },
                  { icon: "ð¤", title: "Referral Partner Revenue", value: "20% commission", desc: "Agencies refer clients; earn 20% recurring for 12 months. Organic CAC reduction and network effect. [assumption]", color: D.green },
                  { icon: "ð", title: "Audit Report Marketplace", value: "$29 one-time", desc: "Sell standalone audit reports to users who don't want a subscription. One-time purchase funneled toward trial. [assumption]", color: D.blue },
                ].map(r => (
                  <div key={r.title} style={{ background: D.card, border: `1px solid ${D.border}`, borderRadius: 14, padding: 22 }}>
                    <div style={{ fontSize: 28, marginBottom: 8 }}>{r.icon}</div>
                    <div style={{ fontWeight: 700, fontSize: 14, color: D.slate1, marginBottom: 4 }}>{r.title}</div>
                    <div style={{ fontSize: 15, fontWeight: 800, color: r.color, marginBottom: 8 }}>{r.value}</div>
                    <div style={{ fontSize: 12, color: D.slate2, lineHeight: 1.6 }}>{r.desc}</div>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>
          )}

          {/* ââââââââââââââââââââââ RISKS TAB ââââââââââââââââââââââââ */}
          {tab === "Risks" && (
            <div>
              <div style={{ display: "grid", gridTemplateColumns: "1fr 1fr", gap: 16, marginBottom: 28 }}>
                <RiskCard level="High" title="Microsoft Clarity + Free Tools Ceiling" desc="Microsoft Clarity is completely free with unlimited sessions, heatmaps, and AI summaries. It trains 50M+ site owners to expect $0 for behavior data. CRObot must justify its premium over 'free' by delivering fix recommendations, not just data â but this is a constant positioning challenge." mitigation="Focus relentlessly on the 'recommendations' gap: Clarity shows the problem; CRObot solves it. Position as Clarity's natural upgrade, not a competitor." />
                <RiskCard level="High" title="Well-Funded Competitor Response" desc="Hotjar (Contentsquare), VWO, or Unbounce could add AI fix recommendations to their existing platforms within 6-12 months. Hotjar especially has the audience (1.2M sites) and the budget (Contentsquare-backed) to build this feature." mitigation="Move fast: ship white-label and agency features before competitors build recommendations. Build switching costs through audit history, team collaboration, and integrations that incumbents won't prioritize for SMBs." />
                <RiskCard level="High" title="AI Hallucinations in Recommendations" desc="Claude may generate CRO suggestions that are confidently wrong â recommending changes that hurt conversions based on surface-level page analysis without understanding the business context, target audience, or conversion goals of the specific page." mitigation="Implement confidence scoring and 'CRObot assumes...' caveats on all AI suggestions. Allow user to input business context (target audience, conversion goal) before auditing for improved accuracy. A/B test recommendation quality." />
                <RiskCard level="Medium" title="AI / API Cost Overrun at Scale" desc="At $29/mo Starter with 5 audits/mo, AI API cost is ~$0.015 total â negligible. But if users on unlimited Pro plans run 200+ audits/month, AI costs could erode margins. One 'viral' campaign sending 10K audits/day could produce unexpected bills." mitigation="Implement hard audit limits per plan (not 'unlimited' on MVP launch). Monitor API spend per user. Cache identical URL audits for 24 hours. Upgrade to cheaper model for low-tier users where appropriate." />
                <RiskCard level="Medium" title="Page Scraping Reliability" desc="Many pages use JavaScript rendering, authentication walls, bot detection (Cloudflare), or anti-scraping measures. If CRObot can't scrape 20% of submitted URLs (Shopify stores, React SPAs, gated content), user frustration leads to churn." mitigation="Build multiple scraping fallbacks: Playwright for JS-heavy pages, browser extension mode for authenticated pages. Be transparent with error messages. Prioritize Shopify/WordPress compatibility in MVP." />
                <RiskCard level="Medium" title="Data Privacy / GDPR Compliance" desc="CRObot scrapes and temporarily stores page content including any user-visible personal data. EU customers expect GDPR compliance. Scraping competitor pages may create IP/copyright edge cases in some jurisdictions." mitigation="Retain scraped page data maximum 30 days with explicit deletion flow. Legal review before EU launch. Audit only public pages (no authenticated/gated content). Consult EU legal counsel on scraping legality before EU marketing push." />
                <RiskCard level="Low" title="SMB Churn in Economic Downturns" desc="Small businesses cancel software subscriptions first during revenue pressure. A recession could increase churn from 3.5% to 6-8% monthly, dramatically compressing LTV and requiring higher customer acquisition to maintain MRR growth." mitigation="Build annual billing incentives aggressively: offer 3 months free on annual. Once a customer has audit history and fix tracking in CRObot, switching cost increases. Focus on demonstrable ROI (show them money saved vs. agency fees)." />
                <RiskCard level="Low" title="Market Saturation from AI Side Projects" desc="Low barrier to build a basic GPT-4o-powered URL auditor means many hobbyist/indie products in this space (some already exist as free tools). Race to bottom on price possible if the market gets crowded with free clones." mitigation="Differentiate on depth (80+ checks, not 10), copy rewrite quality, team collaboration, and integrations â features that take 6+ months to build seriously and can't be replicated in a weekend side project." />
              </div>

              {/* Final Verdict */}
              <div style={{ background: D.card, border: `1px solid ${D.border}`, borderRadius: 14, padding: 28 }}>
                <h3 style={{ margin: "0 0 20px 0", fontSize: 18, fontWeight: 800, color: D.slate1 }}>ð Final Verdict â Scored Assessment</h3>
                <div style={{ display: "grid", gridTemplateColumns: "1fr 1fr", gap: 16, marginBottom: 24 }}>
                  {[
                    { dim: "Market Opportunity", score: 8, note: "Real $1.7B+ market, 68% SMBs underserved, strong growth tailwinds" },
                    { dim: "Competitive Position", score: 7, note: "Clear gap in SMB AI audit space; free tool threat (Clarity) is real but manageable" },
                    { dim: "Revenue Potential", score: 8, note: "$16.5K MRR in Month 12 is conservative; agency tier unlocks higher LTV" },
                    { dim: "Build Complexity", score: 8, note: "URL scraping + AI analysis is technically achievable in 8 weeks on Boldteq stack" },
                    { dim: "Team Fit", score: 8, note: "Next.js + Supabase + Claude API + Stripe = exact Boldteq standard stack" },
                    { dim: "Time to Revenue", score: 8, note: "8-week MVP, Product Hunt launch, first $1K MRR possible by week 10 [assumption]" },
                  ].map(d => (
                    <div key={d.dim}>
                      <div style={{ display: "flex", justifyContent: "space-between", marginBottom: 6 }}>
                        <span style={{ fontSize: 13, fontWeight: 600, color: D.slate1 }}>{d.dim}</span>
                        <span style={{ fontSize: 13, fontWeight: 800, color: D.purple }}>{d.score}/10</span>
                      </div>
                      <div style={{ background: D.bg, borderRadius: 6, height: 8, marginBottom: 4 }}>
                        <div style={{ background: `linear-gradient(90deg, ${D.purple}, ${D.purpleM})`, borderRadius: 6, height: 8, width: `${d.score * 10}%` }} />
                      </div>
                      <div style={{ fontSize: 11, color: D.slate3 }}>{d.note}</div>
                    </div>
                  ))}
                </div>

                {/* Overall Score */}
                <div style={{ background: `linear-gradient(135deg, ${D.purple}, #c026d3)`, borderRadius: 14, padding: 28, color: "#fff" }}>
                  <div style={{ display: "flex", alignItems: "center", gap: 20, flexWrap: "wrap" }}>
                    <div>
                      <div style={{ fontSize: 48, fontWeight: 900, lineHeight: 1 }}>7.8</div>
                      <div style={{ fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 600, opacity: 0.9 }}>out of 10</div>
                    </div>
                    <div style={{ flex: 1, minWidth: 200 }}>
                      <div style={{ fontSize: 20, fontWeight: 800, marginBottom: 8 }}>â GO â Build It</div>
                      <p style={{ margin: 0, fontSize: 13, lineHeight: 1.7, color: "rgba(255,255,255,0.9)" }}>
                        CRObot fills a real, documented gap between free tools (Clarity, Hotjar free) that show data without fixes, and expensive enterprise tools ($300-$1000+/mo) that require setup and analysis expertise. The Claude API makes genuinely intelligent fix recommendations possible at $0.003/audit, enabling a $29/mo price point that's economically viable. The Boldteq stack (Next.js + Supabase + Railway + Claude) means 8-week MVP is achievable. Primary risk is Hotjar/Clarity adding AI suggestions â move fast, build agency moat early. <strong>Launch in under 90 days.</strong>
                      </p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          )}

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}

